 v75.0 improvements [2026-06-12]:
   1. G8.5P BTC-CROSSPAIR DEAD-GATE FIX (critical bug since v60.0): G8.5P at line ~8499
      used `self._quant_layer_close_buf.get("BTCUSDT", [])` — but `_quant_layer_close_buf`
      is a MODULE-LEVEL global dict (line ~1817), NOT a self instance attribute. Since
      `self._quant_layer_close_buf` was NEVER assigned in __init__ or wire_all(), this raised
      AttributeError every single call, caught silently by except → gate dead since v60.0.
      Fix: direct module-level access `_quant_layer_close_buf.get("BTCUSDT", [])` [v75.0].
   2. G8.5Y ATR-VOLCOMPRESS DEAD-GATE FIX (critical bug since v65.0): G8.5Y at line ~8675
      used `getattr(self, "_quant_layer_close_buf", {})` — same class of bug. `getattr`
      returned `{}` (the default) since no instance attribute exists → `.get(symbol)` always
      returned None → gate loop body never reached → gate silently dead since v65.0.
      Fix: direct module-level access `_quant_layer_close_buf` (same pattern as G8.5Z/T/w).
   3. G8.5E QUANT CROSS-SIGNAL COHERENCE GATE (40th gate, +2.0/+0.8/-1.5pts): New soft-gate
      measuring agreement among 3 independent quant systems: (1) OFI z-score direction,
      (2) HMM regime state direction, (3) BTC GEX net direction vs trade direction.
      3/3 aligned → +2.0pts (ultra-conviction institutional coherence);
      2/3 aligned → +0.8pts (majority alignment confirmation);
      0/3 aligned → -1.5pts (all 3 systems oppose the signal direction — major headwind).
      Uses existing data already computed in the evaluation cycle — zero extra API calls.
      Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS/_record() [v75.0].
   4. KELLY STEP 34: CROSS-SIGNAL COHERENCE SIZING: When G8.5E fires 3/3 (all quant systems
      agree with direction) → Kelly ×1.06 (amplify high-conviction coherent trades); when
      G8.5E fires 0/3 (all 3 oppose) → Kelly ×0.87 (strongly de-size against-signal trades).
      Uses `self._last_g85e_votes` stored during G8.5E evaluation. Non-fatal [v75.0].
   5. `gate_g85dv` EXPLICIT INIT: Added explicit `_gate_stats` + `_gate_stats_recent` init
      entries for `gate_g85dv` (DGRP-Velocity G8.5X gate) which relied on `_record()`
      setdefault — now explicitly initialized alongside all other gates [v75.0].
 v74.0 improvements [2026-06-12]:
   1. F78 VOL_EXPANSION_FLAG ALWAYS-0 FIX (critical bug): The vol_expansion_flag feature
      injected at G4 (for NN v13 F78) used `getattr(self, "_quant_layer_close_buf", {})` —
      but `_quant_layer_close_buf` is a MODULE-LEVEL global dict (line ~1783), not a `self`
      attribute. `getattr(self, ...)` always returned `{}` → F78 always 0.0 → NN v13 had a
      permanently-dead vol-expansion input. Fixed by directly accessing the module-level
      global `_quant_layer_close_buf` (same pattern used by G8.5P at line ~8457) [v74.0].
   2. "36-GATE SIGNAL FILTER" STALE BOOT STRING FIX: The boot capability stamp log line
      still printed "36-GATE SIGNAL FILTER" despite v73.0 reaching 38 gates (v74.0=39 gates).
      Root cause: the string literal was not captured by the sed replacement that updated
      gate counts elsewhere. Fixed to "39-GATE SIGNAL FILTER" [v74.0].
   3. KEY GATES HEADER STALE VERSION FIX: The KEY GATES docstring header still said "v72.0"
      despite v73.0 adding G8.5C. Updated to v74.0 and added Kelly31/32/33 entries [v74.0].
   4. G8.5D OFI-VELOCITY GATE (39th gate, ±2.0pts): New soft-gate tracking signed rate-of-
      change (velocity) of the per-symbol OFI z-score across consecutive scan cycles. When OFI
      is accelerating in the trade direction (velocity > 0.5σ) → +2.0pts surging institutional
      flow. When decelerating against direction (velocity < -0.5σ) → -1.5pts fading flow signal.
      Tracks last 2 OFI z-score readings per symbol in `_ofi_velocity_buf` (deque maxlen=2).
      Guard: both readings must be within 90s of current time; |delta| < 10.0 (noise guard).
      Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS/_record() [v74.0].
   5. G9 FLOW-PERSISTENCE STACK BONUS (+1.0pts): When G8.5B OFI-Persistence fires at its
      maximum strength (+2.0pts, 3/3 aligned) AND G8.5C Regime-Coherence also fires at maximum
      (+2.0pts, dual HMM+GEX confirm) in the same signal evaluation, a compound +1.0pt "stack
      bonus" is added to quality_score. The simultaneous agreement of persistent order-flow AND
      institutional regime coherence represents a very rare high-conviction state that is
      statistically unlikely to occur by chance [v74.0].
   6. KELLY STEP 33 — ENSEMBLE DIRECTION CONFIDENCE SCALE: Uses the NN trainer's last 3-model
      ensemble agreement to size position. When all 3 tree ensemble models (HistGBT + ExtraTrees
      + RF) predict the same direction AND NN uncertainty < 0.10 → Kelly ×1.07 (confirmed
      conviction). When NN uncertainty ≥ 0.15 (uncertain/conflicted state) → Kelly ×0.90
      (de-size when model is confused). Reuses `nn_trainer._last_uncertainty` (already computed
      by MC-Dropout inference). Guard: nn_trainer must exist and be trained; stacks AFTER Step
      32; non-fatal [v74.0].
 v73.0 improvements [2026-06-12]:
   1. F76-F80 NN FEATURE INJECTION FIX (critical bug): All 5 new v72.0 NN features
      (ofi_persistence_score, regime_coherence_score, vol_expansion_flag,
      hmm_expansion_prob_norm, spread_regime_flag) were returning 0.0 defaults on every
      inference call because the values were never stamped into signal_data before
      predict_from_dict(). Now injected at G4 stamping block: OFI z-score from timing
      state, OFI persistence from ring, regime coherence from HMM+GEX, vol expansion
      from BTC close buffer, spread flag from rolling 20-bar median [v73.0].
   2. G8.5B OFI_Z SOURCE FIX (critical bug): G8.5B reads signal_data["ofi_z"] but this
      key was never set in signal_data — gate always got 0.0 → never recorded directional
      OFI readings → 3-cycle ring always empty → gate was completely dead. Fixed by
      injecting signal_data["ofi_z"] from timing_state.ofi_zscore() at the same G4
      stamping block, making the value available to G8.5B downstream [v73.0].
   3. G8.5C REGIME-COHERENCE GATE (38th gate, ±2.0pts): New soft-gate checking dual
      institutional confirmation from HMM regime + BTC GEX net direction. When both
      EXPANSION+GEX-bullish align with BUY, or CONTRACTION+GEX-bearish align with SELL
      → +2.0pts strong dual-confirm. Both against direction → -2.0pts. Single source
      aligned → ±1.0pts weak. Threshold: GEX net > $200M; HMM P≥0.60; ≥15 HMM samples
      required (cold-start safe). Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS
      /_record(). Targets the majority of false signals that lack cross-source institutional
      validation and improves WR by ensuring HMM + dealer GEX both agree [v73.0].
   4. KELLY STEP 32 — OFI-PERSIST SIZING SCALE: When the 3-cycle OFI ring shows 3/3
      readings aligned with direction (persistent institutional flow) → Kelly ×1.08
      (confirmed directional conviction, validated by G8.5B gate data). When 0/3 readings
      aligned (persistent adverse flow) → Kelly ×0.88 (de-size against flow headwind).
      Reuses G8.5B ring data (no extra computation). Non-fatal; stacks AFTER Step 31 [v73.0].
   5. CPCV CHANCE-FLOOR GUARD TIGHTENING (neural_signal_trainer): CPCV threshold push
      floor raised from avg>47% → avg>50%. At avg=47.5% the model is essentially at
      chance; the previous floor allowed the push to fire aggressively (gap=18.8% →
      threshold 0.540→0.560). Raising to 50% prevents threshold overshoot when CPCV
      folds are near-chance. Push multiplier also reduced 0.30→0.25 to dampen drift [v73.0].
   6. _SPREAD_MEDIAN_BUF tracker: Per-symbol rolling 20-bar bid-ask spread median deque
      for F80 spread_regime_flag computation. Previously no rolling baseline existed so
      F80 always returned 0.0 even when spread was elevated [v73.0].
 v72.0 improvements [2026-06-12]:
   1. G8.5B OFI PERSISTENCE GATE (37th gate, ±2.0pts): New soft-gate tracking per-symbol
      order-flow imbalance (OFI) direction over 3 consecutive scan cycles. When OFI has
      been consistently aligned with the signal direction for all readings → +2.0pts
      persistent-flow confirmation. All readings opposed → -2.0pts adverse-flow headwind.
      2/3 aligned → +0.5pts mild confirmation. Guard: ≥2 readings, 45s min update interval.
      Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS/_record() [v72.0].
