  v67.0 IMPROVEMENTS: NN-QUAL-GATE-28% | ADAPTIVE-MAX-CLASS-WEIGHT | CPCV-GAP-7% | G4-HARD-CAP-0.52 | G4-DEADZONE-0.42 | COMPOUND-CAP-0.52:
  v66.0 IMPROVEMENTS: G4-DEADZONE-RELIEF | OPENROUTER-SESSION-PERM-DISABLE | EV-CRISIS-FLOOR-4.5 | G8.5X-DGRP-VELOCITY | KELLY-STEP28-MAXDD-BRAKE:
    1. G4 DEAD-ZONE EMERGENCY RELIEF (start_unity_engine.py):
       Tracks last 15 G4 pass/fail results in _g4_pass_ring. When all 15 fail (dead-zone),
       reduces nn_threshold by min(0.09, threshold−0.44), floor = 0.44. Prevents the NN
       learned-pessimism deadlock at WR=29% where Sharpe-tightening cascades push threshold
       to 0.56–0.58 while NN predictions cluster at 0.30–0.42. INFO log on activation [v66.0].
    2. OPENROUTER SESSION-PERMANENT DISABLE (godmod3_strategy.py):
       After GenericErrGuard fires (≥12 consecutive generic errors → 2h disable), the model
       is also added to _session_perm_disabled and never retried for the rest of the session.
       _is_model_disabled() checks this set first. Eliminates 2h-disable→re-enable→fail loop
       for dead routes (claude-fable-5/mythos-5 404 every call) [v66.0].
    3. EV CRISIS FLOOR — SHARPE < -4.5 TIER (start_unity_engine.py):
       New tier between existing -3.5 (1.20×) and -5.0 (1.35×): Sharpe < -4.5 → EV floor
       1.28× EV_MIN_THRESHOLD. At current Sharpe=-4.87 this raises the floor from 1.20×
       to 1.28× (35.8bps), tightening G0 in deep-crisis regimes [v66.0].
    4. G8.5X DGRP-VELOCITY GATE (start_unity_engine.py) — 35th gate:
       Tracks rolling GEX DGRP score history (deque maxlen=6, 30s update guard). Velocity =
       current_dgrp − mean of 3 prior readings. Rapid deterioration (velocity < −8pts): −2.0pts
       quality. Rapid improvement (velocity > +6pts): +1.5pts quality. Wired to gate_stats/
       _GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS/_record() [v66.0].
    5. KELLY STEP 28 — MaxDD EMERGENCY BRAKE (start_unity_engine.py):
       Hard absolute Kelly cap when MaxDD enters ruin territory, applied AFTER DD-scale step.
       MaxDD > 50%: cap = 0.2% (preservation mode). MaxDD > 45%: cap = 0.4% (emergency).
       INFO log on activation. Prevents further capital destruction in sustained ruin [v66.0].
  v65.0 IMPROVEMENTS: G8.5Y ATR-VOLCOMPRESS GATE | KELLY STEP 27 SORTINO-SCALE | G8.5S FLIP-ZONE DOUBLE | G9 SORTINO-FLOOR | NN ENSEMBLE COHERENCE:
    1. G8.5Y ATR VOLATILITY COMPRESSION GATE (start_unity_engine.py) — 34th gate:
       Rolling ATR percentile (bar-to-bar absolute return proxy, ≥20 bars, 60-bar window).
       Compressed ATR (≤25th pct) = pre-breakout conditions: +2.0pts to quality_score.
       Expanded ATR (≥80th pct) = noisy high-vol market: −1.5pts to quality_score.
       25–80th pct range = gate silent. Non-fatal, soft-gate (quality adjuster only).
       Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS/_record() [v65.0].
    2. KELLY STEP 27 — SORTINO DOWNSIDE PROTECTION SCALE (start_unity_engine.py):
       Sortino ratio < -2.5 (extreme downside vol) → Kelly × 0.85 (de-risk).
       Sortino ratio > 2.0 + ring WR > 35% (confirmed downside-controlled edge) → Kelly × 1.05.
       Non-fatal, capped at _kelly_ceil. Complements Step 24 (Calmar/Sharpe CB) [v65.0].
    3. G8.5S SPREAD-STRESS FLIP-ZONE DOUBLE PENALTY (start_unity_engine.py):
       In GEX FLIP ZONE (maximum dealer hedging uncertainty), spread widening is doubly
       destructive (wider fills + amplified stop-hunting). Penalties doubled in FLIP:
       FLIP + spread>3×mean: −4pts (was −2pts); FLIP + spread>2×mean: −2pts (was −1pt).
       Normal (non-FLIP) penalties unchanged [v65.0].
    4. G9 SORTINO ULTRA-CRISIS FLOOR (start_unity_engine.py):
       When Sortino ratio < −4.0 (extreme downside-vol regime, ≥15 ring samples):
       G9 floor raised +1pt (capped at SIGNAL_MIN_QUALITY_GATE+4). Sortino < −4.0 is
       orthogonal to Sharpe (catches high-loss-magnitude regimes that Sharpe misses) [v65.0].
    5. NN ENSEMBLE COHERENCE BOOST/PENALTY (neural_signal_trainer.py):
       After unified 3-way tree consensus blend: compute range of all active model outputs
       (MLP/Transformer base, HistGBT, ExtraTrees). When all agree within ±3pp → high
       ensemble confidence → base_prob × 1.02 boost (cap 0.95). When range > 15pp →
       ensemble disagreement → slight penalty × 0.99 (floor 0.05) [v65.0].
  v64.0 IMPROVEMENTS: G8.5Z AUTOCORRELATION GATE | KELLY STEP 26 DUAL-REGIME | UNIFIED 3-WAY TREE CONSENSUS:
    1. G8.5Z RETURN-AUTOCORRELATION PERSISTENCE GATE (start_unity_engine.py) — 33rd gate:
       Lag-1 autocorrelation of bar returns from _quant_layer_close_buf (≥20 bars required).
       Positive AC (>+0.15) = trending regime: rewards trend-following entries, penalises fades.
       Negative AC (<-0.15) = mean-reverting regime: rewards fade entries (buy-dip/sell-rip).
       |AC| ≤ 0.15 = random walk → gate silent. Scoring:
         Trending+aligned: +2.0pts | Trending+counter: -1.5pts
         Mean-rev+fade:    +1.5pts | Mean-rev+chasing: -1.0pt
       Reference: De Prado AFML ch.17 — AC is the primary discriminator between
       trending and mean-reverting microstructures. Soft-gate (quality adjuster only).
       Wired to gate_stats/_GATE_DISPLAY_LABELS/_SOFT_GATE_KEYS [v64.0].
    2. KELLY STEP 26 — HMM-GEX DUAL REGIME CONVICTION UPSCALE (start_unity_engine.py):
       When BOTH HMM regime AND BTC GEX net direction simultaneously confirm signal direction:
         EXPANSION P≥0.75 + GEX net > +$1B + BUY:  Kelly × 1.10
         CONTRACTION P≥0.65 + GEX net < −$1B + SELL: Kelly × 1.10
       Cap: Kelly × min(1.10×, _kelly_ceil). Two orthogonal regime sources agreeing means
       the edge assumption in Kelly's f* is MORE reliable → justified modest upscale [v64.0].
    3. UNIFIED 3-WAY TREE CONSENSUS BLEND (neural_signal_trainer.py):
       When HistGBT + ExtraTrees are both fitted, compute accuracy-weighted tree consensus
       FIRST, then blend as single tree component vs neural base (prevents double-counting).
       Total tree weight capped at 40% to preserve neural-net dominance [v64.0].
